    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="0738" n="730" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760F.62/1884</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-05">November 5, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: As of possible interest
                    and for your information, I am forwarding you, hereto attached, a memorandum,
                    summarizing my observations, from the Warsaw angle, on the far-reaching <pb
                        facs="0739" n="731" xml:id="pg731"/> repercussions of this Munich Conference
                    and its immediate sequel.</p>
                <p>This memorandum is a copy of the substance of a letter I have sent the
                    President—and pressure of work in this office prevents my making a separate and
                    “clean” copy for you at this moment. I therefore do hope that you will forgive
                    me, under the circumstances.</p>
                <p>With every good wish and renewed congratulations on the wonderful work you are
                    doing I am,</p>
                <p>Yours faithfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anthony Biddle,
                    Jr.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d709-a1.xml" xpointer="d709-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
